    <!-- Haven round 9, launcher icon ONLY. REPLACES round 7's
         gradient foreground outright — same segmented-house
         design, same 30..78 x 30..76 envelope, but SOLID FLAT
         facet colors and NO <gradient> elements anywhere.
         WHY (device-proven, 2026-11-03 20:34 video): on the
         user's Fold8, the round-7 adaptive icon rendered the
         cream field + solid yellow sparkle ONLY — the five
         gradient-filled house paths did not render in the
         device's adaptive-icon path (the shipped legacy PNGs
         DID contain the house, pixel-verified, so the failure
         is vector-gradient-specific, not a missing resource).
         Solid fills are the renderer-proof construction: every
         path here is a flat fillColor, exactly like the
         sparkle that did render.
         FACETS (same envelope as round 7, so the safe-zone
         discipline carries over unchanged):
         - Roof, each side split into TWO flats along the
           y=41 midline: lime #9BF67C ridge triangle at the
           apex, deep leaf #3E6B2F eave trapezoid below. The
           outer edges stay deep leaf (crisp on cream, ~6:1);
           lime never touches cream directly — it is an
           interior highlight bounded by deep leaf, exactly as
           round 7's gradient direction intended.
         - Body left (36..50) and right (62..72): mid green
           #66BB6A flats.
         - Center panel (50..62): TWO flats — yellow #FFD54F
           top half (52..64), orange #FF8F00 bottom half
           (64..76) — the warm center, no vertical gradient.
         - Door (39..47, arch apex ~61, base 76): cream
           #FAF7F0, drawn after the body so it reads as a
           doorway; on the LEFT, as the reference.
         - Sparkle: yellow #FFD54F 4-point star centered
           (71,37), half-size 6, clear of the roof edge.
         SAFE ZONE (center 54,54): outermost ink unchanged
         from round 7 (under ~30.7dp), so circle, squircle,
         square, rectangle, and expressive masks (including
         Samsung's default shape) never clip critical content.
         RECENTS (the stated acceptance case): if a device
         path blackens the cream background layer, the bright
         flat facets still read — lime, yellow, orange, and
         cream doorway on black, deep-leaf eaves bounded by
         bright neighbors. The legacy mipmap PNGs render the
         same flats (see make-legacy-icon-round9.py).
         Monochrome (ic_launcher_monochrome.xml) is unchanged:
         it was already solid fills and merges the facets into
         one silhouette. Background (cream field) is unchanged. -->
